<title>SOUTH KOREA: SSANGYONG OIL INTERIM NET RISES.</title>
<headline>SSANGYONG OIL INTERIM NET RISES.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>	 (in billion won unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (won)				   1,232 vs 1,131</p>
<p>    Net					    69.4 vs 64.0</p>
<p>    Turnover				  2,472.7 vs 1,963.9</p>
<p>    Profit before tax			 100.2 vs    78.4</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries			     1.9 vs     6.89</p>
<p>Note - Ssangyong Oil Refining Co, a member of Ssangyong Group, is one of the leading oil refiners in South Korea. A company spokesman attributed the rise in profits to an increase in sales of lighter oil products and a drop in foreign exchange losses.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
